\ A live binding of a native's name must not change the effect the native's own raise reports.
\ `victim`'s `-` is pre-resolved to the native before the binding exists, and the binding is live in
\ the file's frame at capture; the row is the native's `( a b -- a-b )`, not the binding's
\ `( a b -- c )`. The binding sits at top level; a marker inside `caller` would block AOT compilation.
\
\ The interpreter, eager, and AOT runs of this program must render the chain frame for frame
\ identically; the AOT suite builds this file through a `.source` redirect and diffs the same golden.

victim: ( -- x ) [ "x" 40.0 - 1.0 + ] ;
caller: ( -- x ) [ victim 2.0 + ] ;
-: override ( a b -- c ) [ drop drop 99.0 ] ;
caller .
